2026-09-10 18:47:18,934 | INFO | rag.vectorstore | QDRANT POINT: id=9cffe155c3654f19919f7c37bfb159a7 payload={'text': 'Acme Corporation\n Finance — Expense & Procurement Policy\n Document ID: ACME-POL-FIN-009  |  Version: 1.6  |  Effective Date: April 1, 2026  |  Classification: Internal Use Only\n1. Purpose\nThis policy governs how Acme employees request, approve, and report business expenses and how\npurchases of goods and services are procured on behalf of the company.\n2. Expense Approval Thresholds\nExpense Amount\nRequired Approval\nTurnaround Target\nUnder $100\nAuto-approved, manager notified\nImmediate\n$100 - $999\nDirect manager approval\n2 business days\n$1,000 - $9,999\nDirector approval\n3 business days\n$10,000 - $49,999\nVP approval + Finance review\n5 business days\n$50,000 and above\nCFO approval + Procurement committee\n10 business days\n3. Travel Expense Guidelines\n\x7f Airfare must be booked in economy class for flights under 6 hours; premium economy is permitted for\nflights over 6 hours with director approval.\n\x7f Hotel expenses are reimbursed up to $275 per night in major metro areas and $180 per night', 'metadata': {'producer': 'ReportLab PDF Library - (opensource)', 'creator': '(unspecified)', 'creationdate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'author': '(anonymous)', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'subject': '(unspecified)', 'title': '(anonymous)', 'trapped': '/False', 'source': 'Acme_Corp_Finance_Expense_Procurement_Policy.pdf', 'total_pages': 2, 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'file_path': 'corpora\\Acme_Corp_Finance_Expense_Procurement_Policy.pdf', 'file_type': '.pdf', 'source_type': 'unknown', 'ingestion_time': '2026-09-10T13:17:18.813484+00:00', 'content_length': 1617, 'word_count': 249, 'document_id': '6ad708307df8f85e', 'chunk_id': '6ad708307df8f85e_chunk_1', 'chunk_index': 1}}
2026-09-10 18:47:18,934 | INFO | rag.vectorstore | QDRANT POINT: id=e0724f8da02a44b7ba795fbff6d956e7 payload={'text': 'flights over 6 hours with director approval.\n\x7f Hotel expenses are reimbursed up to $275 per night in major metro areas and $180 per night\nelsewhere, receipts required for all amounts.\n\x7f Meal per diem is $75 per day domestic and $95 per day international, itemized receipts not required\nunder $25.\n\x7f Ground transportation should default to public transit or rideshare economy tiers; luxury rideshare\ntiers are not reimbursable.\n4. Corporate Card Policy\nEmployees with a recurring business travel need may request a corporate card through Finance Ops. All\ncorporate card transactions must be reconciled in the Expensify system within 15 calendar days of the\ntransaction date. Cards not reconciled within 45 days are automatically suspended pending manager\nreview.', 'metadata': {'producer': 'ReportLab PDF Library - (opensource)', 'creator': '(unspecified)', 'creationdate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'author': '(anonymous)', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'subject': '(unspecified)', 'title': '(anonymous)', 'trapped': '/False', 'source': 'Acme_Corp_Finance_Expense_Procurement_Policy.pdf', 'total_pages': 2, 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'file_path': 'corpora\\Acme_Corp_Finance_Expense_Procurement_Policy.pdf', 'file_type': '.pdf', 'source_type': 'unknown', 'ingestion_time': '2026-09-10T13:17:18.813484+00:00', 'content_length': 1617, 'word_count': 249, 'document_id': '6ad708307df8f85e', 'chunk_id': '6ad708307df8f85e_chunk_2', 'chunk_index': 2}}
2026-09-10 18:47:18,935 | INFO | rag.vectorstore | QDRANT POINT: id=8834938b8bd948fda74182ee9f905226 payload={'text': '5. Software and SaaS Procurement\nAll new software purchases, including free-tier signups that may later convert to paid plans, must be\nlogged in the Software Asset Registry and reviewed by IT Security for data handling and vendor risk before\npurchase, regardless of dollar amount. This applies in addition to, not instead of, the standard expense\napproval thresholds in Section 2. Procurement of any tool that will process Confidential or Restricted data\n(as classified in the IT Security Policy, ACME-POL-IT-014) requires a completed vendor security\nquestionnaire prior to approval.\n6. Prohibited Expenses\n\x7f Personal entertainment, gym memberships, or spa services.\n\x7f Alcohol at a value exceeding $50 per event when client entertainment is involved.\n\x7f Traffic violations, parking tickets, or other fines incurred during business travel.\n\x7f First-class airfare under any circumstance without CFO pre-approval.\n7. Audit and Non-Compliance', 'metadata': {'producer': 'ReportLab PDF Library - (opensource)', 'creator': '(unspecified)', 'creationdate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'author': '(anonymous)', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'subject': '(unspecified)', 'title': '(anonymous)', 'trapped': '/False', 'source': 'Acme_Corp_Finance_Expense_Procurement_Policy.pdf', 'total_pages': 2, 'page': 1, 'page_label': '2', 'file_path': 'corpora\\Acme_Corp_Finance_Expense_Procurement_Policy.pdf', 'file_type': '.pdf', 'source_type': 'unknown', 'ingestion_time': '2026-09-10T13:17:18.813484+00:00', 'content_length': 1392, 'word_count': 197, 'document_id': '6ad708307df8f85e', 'chunk_id': '6ad708307df8f85e_chunk_3', 'chunk_index': 3}}
