2026-09-10 18:47:19,125 | INFO | rag.vectorstore | QDRANT POINT: id=4150a1c1d485476e8cd3c9b261355e8d payload={'text': "Acme Corporation\n Human Resources — Remote Work & Home Office Equipment Policy\nDocument ID: ACME-POL-HR-007  |  Version: 2.1  |  Effective Date: March 3, 2026  |  Classification: Internal Use Only\n1. Purpose\nThis policy defines eligibility, expectations, and equipment support for employees who work remotely on a\nfull-time, hybrid, or occasional basis. It is administered by Human Resources in coordination with the IT\nHelpdesk and People Managers.\n2. Eligibility and Work Arrangements\nEmployees may request one of three arrangements, subject to manager approval: Fully Remote (no\nregular office attendance required), Hybrid (minimum 2 days per week in an Acme office), or Office-Based\n(5 days per week on-site). Remote work eligibility is reviewed at the start of each fiscal year and may be\nrevoked if role requirements change.\n3. Core Working Hours and Availability\nRemote and hybrid employees must be reachable via Slack and calendar during their team's designated", 'metadata': {'producer': 'ReportLab PDF Library - (opensource)', 'creator': '(unspecified)', 'creationdate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'author': '(anonymous)', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'subject': '(unspecified)', 'title': '(anonymous)', 'trapped': '/False', 'source': 'Acme_Corp_HR_Remote_Work_Policy.pdf', 'total_pages': 2, 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'file_path': 'corpora\\Acme_Corp_HR_Remote_Work_Policy.pdf', 'file_type': '.pdf', 'source_type': 'unknown', 'ingestion_time': '2026-09-10T13:17:18.992606+00:00', 'content_length': 2135, 'word_count': 323, 'document_id': '5cdd36da112c24b7', 'chunk_id': '5cdd36da112c24b7_chunk_1', 'chunk_index': 1}}
2026-09-10 18:47:19,125 | INFO | rag.vectorstore | QDRANT POINT: id=5bc2a4fe41d0435ba662014301be7c90 payload={'text': "revoked if role requirements change.\n3. Core Working Hours and Availability\nRemote and hybrid employees must be reachable via Slack and calendar during their team's designated\ncore hours, typically 10:00 AM to 3:00 PM local time, regardless of arrangement. Employees working\nacross time zones from their team should agree on an overlap window with their manager in writing.\n4. Home Office Equipment and Stipend\nAcme provides a one-time home office setup stipend of $750 for newly remote or hybrid employees,\ncovering desks, chairs, and monitors. In addition, employees receive an ongoing monthly remote work\nstipend of $85 to offset internet and utility costs. Stipend requests are submitted through the Workday\nExpense module under category 'Remote Equipment.'\n\x7f Company-issued laptop, keyboard, and mouse remain Acme property and must be returned upon\nseparation.\n\x7f Employees are responsible for maintaining a private, secure internet connection with a minimum of\n25 Mbps download speed.", 'metadata': {'producer': 'ReportLab PDF Library - (opensource)', 'creator': '(unspecified)', 'creationdate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'author': '(anonymous)', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'subject': '(unspecified)', 'title': '(anonymous)', 'trapped': '/False', 'source': 'Acme_Corp_HR_Remote_Work_Policy.pdf', 'total_pages': 2, 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'file_path': 'corpora\\Acme_Corp_HR_Remote_Work_Policy.pdf', 'file_type': '.pdf', 'source_type': 'unknown', 'ingestion_time': '2026-09-10T13:17:18.992606+00:00', 'content_length': 2135, 'word_count': 323, 'document_id': '5cdd36da112c24b7', 'chunk_id': '5cdd36da112c24b7_chunk_2', 'chunk_index': 2}}
2026-09-10 18:47:19,125 | INFO | rag.vectorstore | QDRANT POINT: id=2d4ac855dc5a4d1199fb5700636cab66 payload={'text': 'separation.\n\x7f Employees are responsible for maintaining a private, secure internet connection with a minimum of\n25 Mbps download speed.\n\x7f Personal printers, webcams, and headsets are eligible for stipend reimbursement up to $150\ncombined per calendar year.\n5. Remote Work and Network Security Requirements\nEmployees working outside an Acme office must connect to company systems using the\ncompany-approved VPN client at all times when accessing internal applications. Use of public Wi-Fi', 'metadata': {'producer': 'ReportLab PDF Library - (opensource)', 'creator': '(unspecified)', 'creationdate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'author': '(anonymous)', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-08-24T09:44:48+00:00', 'subject': '(unspecified)', 'title': '(anonymous)', 'trapped': '/False', 'source': 'Acme_Corp_HR_Remote_Work_Policy.pdf', 'total_pages': 2, 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'file_path': 'corpora\\Acme_Corp_HR_Remote_Work_Policy.pdf', 'file_type': '.pdf', 'source_type': 'unknown', 'ingestion_time': '2026-09-10T13:17:18.992606+00:00', 'content_length': 2135, 'word_count': 323, 'document_id': '5cdd36da112c24b7', 'chunk_id': '5cdd36da112c24b7_chunk_3', 'chunk_index': 3}}
