2026-09-10 18:47:19,364 | INFO | rag.vectorstore | QDRANT POINT: id=abb08752ccd74b28a917c45e826fdd7e payload={'text': "Acme Corporation\n Information Technology Security & Acceptable Use Policy\n Document ID: ACME-POL-IT-014  |  Version: 3.2  |  Effective Date: January 15, 2026  |  Classification: Internal Use\n Only\n1. Purpose and Scope\nThis policy establishes the minimum security standards and acceptable use requirements for all\nemployees, contractors, and third-party vendors who access Acme Corporation's information systems,\nnetworks, and data. It applies to all company-owned and personally owned devices used to conduct\ncompany business, whether on-premises, remote, or hybrid.\nThis document is reviewed annually by the Information Security Office and supersedes all previous\nversions upon publication. Employees are required to acknowledge this policy during onboarding and upon\neach material revision.\n2. Password and Authentication Requirements\nAll employees must comply with the following authentication standards when accessing Acme systems:", 'metadata': {'producer': 'ReportLab PDF Library - (opensource)', 'creator': '(unspecified)', 'creationdate': '2026-08-24T09:17:07+00:00', 'author': '(anonymous)', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-08-24T09:17:07+00:00', 'subject': '(unspecified)', 'title': '(anonymous)', 'trapped': '/False', 'source': 'Acme_Corp_IT_Security_Policy.pdf', 'total_pages': 3, 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'file_path': 'corpora\\Acme_Corp_IT_Security_Policy.pdf', 'file_type': '.pdf', 'source_type': 'unknown', 'ingestion_time': '2026-09-10T13:17:19.202286+00:00', 'content_length': 2093, 'word_count': 289, 'document_id': '96122ae3c175f70e', 'chunk_id': '96122ae3c175f70e_chunk_1', 'chunk_index': 1}}
2026-09-10 18:47:19,365 | INFO | rag.vectorstore | QDRANT POINT: id=954dbc5e853a40dcbf82166b28c18ed7 payload={'text': 'each material revision.\n2. Password and Authentication Requirements\nAll employees must comply with the following authentication standards when accessing Acme systems:\n\x7f Passwords must be a minimum of 14 characters and include at least one uppercase letter, one\nlowercase letter, one number, and one special character.\n\x7f Multi-factor authentication (MFA) is mandatory for all remote access, VPN connections, and cloud\napplication logins (Okta, Google Workspace, AWS Console).\n\x7f Passwords must not be reused across the last 10 password cycles.\n\x7f Shared or generic accounts are prohibited except where explicitly approved by the Information\nSecurity Office for service accounts.\n\x7f Employees must report suspected credential compromise to the Security Operations Center (SOC)\nwithin 1 hour of discovery.\n3. Data Classification Standards\nAll company data must be classified according to the following tiers. Handling, storage, and transmission', 'metadata': {'producer': 'ReportLab PDF Library - (opensource)', 'creator': '(unspecified)', 'creationdate': '2026-08-24T09:17:07+00:00', 'author': '(anonymous)', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-08-24T09:17:07+00:00', 'subject': '(unspecified)', 'title': '(anonymous)', 'trapped': '/False', 'source': 'Acme_Corp_IT_Security_Policy.pdf', 'total_pages': 3, 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'file_path': 'corpora\\Acme_Corp_IT_Security_Policy.pdf', 'file_type': '.pdf', 'source_type': 'unknown', 'ingestion_time': '2026-09-10T13:17:19.202286+00:00', 'content_length': 2093, 'word_count': 289, 'document_id': '96122ae3c175f70e', 'chunk_id': '96122ae3c175f70e_chunk_2', 'chunk_index': 2}}
2026-09-10 18:47:19,365 | INFO | rag.vectorstore | QDRANT POINT: id=8675adc3e3724fd7b5485ff4eeb098cd payload={'text': 'within 1 hour of discovery.\n3. Data Classification Standards\nAll company data must be classified according to the following tiers. Handling, storage, and transmission\nrequirements vary by classification level as summarized below.\nClassification\nDescription\nExamples\nEncryption Required\nPublic\nApproved for external release\nMarketing materials, press releases\nNo\nInternal\nFor employee use only, low sensitivity\nInternal memos, org charts\nNo\nConfidential\nSensitive business information\nFinancial reports, contracts, source code\nYes (at rest & in transit)', 'metadata': {'producer': 'ReportLab PDF Library - (opensource)', 'creator': '(unspecified)', 'creationdate': '2026-08-24T09:17:07+00:00', 'author': '(anonymous)', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-08-24T09:17:07+00:00', 'subject': '(unspecified)', 'title': '(anonymous)', 'trapped': '/False', 'source': 'Acme_Corp_IT_Security_Policy.pdf', 'total_pages': 3, 'page': 0, 'page_label': '1', 'file_path': 'corpora\\Acme_Corp_IT_Security_Policy.pdf', 'file_type': '.pdf', 'source_type': 'unknown', 'ingestion_time': '2026-09-10T13:17:19.202286+00:00', 'content_length': 2093, 'word_count': 289, 'document_id': '96122ae3c175f70e', 'chunk_id': '96122ae3c175f70e_chunk_3', 'chunk_index': 3}}
